cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "msat — MemSat Experimental Harness"
abstract: >-
  An experimental harness that measures how answer accuracy and evidence recall
  change as an LLM agent retrieves K memories under context budget B. The study
  is a crossed K x B factorial: K and B are the swept factors, while the
  embedder, chunking scheme, similarity metric, prompt, and gold position are
  pinned, named, and hashed into every artifact. The primary result is the
  estimated log2(K) x log2(B) interaction term, tested against a pre-registered
  sign prediction. The harness also computes a retriever-independent analytical
  recall ceiling directly from benchmark metadata at zero API cost.
